 Handshake Prototype — Architecture Note\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2038\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nMulti-site local deployments need authenticated node sync without assuming a shared network password. T024 opened for a distributed zero-trust sync path; the first concrete deliverable was a replication handshake between peers.\\n\\n## Prototype (2026-08-06)\\n\\nBob implemented a node-replication handshake so each side must authenticate before accepting sync traffic from the other. That put an Active prototype on the board for T024.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-38\\n\\n# Node Sync Handshake Prototype — Architecture Note\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2038\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nMulti-site local deployments need authenticated node sync without assuming a shared network password. T024 opened for a distributed zero-trust sync path; the first concrete deliverable was a replication handshake between peers.\\n\\n## What this note does not claim\\n\\nNominal-latency validation and any later high-latency failure modes are outside this write-up. As of 2026-08-06 the task was Active on the strength of the prototype alone.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 38 node sync handshak prototyp architectur note owner bob document key doc 2038 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 multi site local deploy need authent node sync without assum a share network password t024 open for a distribut zero trust sync path the first concret deliver wa a replic handshak between peer prototyp 2026 08 06 bob implement a node replic handshak so each side must authent befor accept sync traffic from the other that put an activ prototyp on the board for t024 sourc id src gdoc 38 node sync handshak prototyp architectur note owner bob document key doc 2038 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 multi site local deploy need authent node sync wi