ed-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1197, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:05\", \"token_count\": 534, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## What was prototyped\\n\\nA handshake in which each node presents a signed challenge/response before either side accepts replication traffic from the other. No central node is required to bootstrap trust between two peers.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## Result as of 2026-08-06\\n\\nThe handshake completed reliably across every run on a single LAN segment with nominal round-trip latency. No cross-node encryption mismatches or handshake rejections were seen at that stage.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## Open question\\n\\nThe prototype has only been exercised on one LAN segment. Whether the handshake holds up across a simulated multi-site link with realistic latency and jitter has not been tested and is the planned next step before this can support multi-site rollout.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy what wa prototyp a handshak in which each node present a sign challeng respons befor either side accept replic traffic from the other no central node is requir to bootstrap trust between two peer sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy result a of 2026 08 06 the handshak complet reliabl across everi run on a singl lan segment with nomin round trip latenc no cross node encrypt mismatch or handshak reject were seen at that stage sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy open question the prototyp ha onli been exercis on one lan segment whether the handshak hold up across a simul multi site link with realist latenc and jitter ha not been test and is the plan next step befor this can support multi site rollout\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9dc21828a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\", \"id\": \"4c8ad9d86bb9e4c5\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.25447566019013707, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0491803288430529, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7334981, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9dc21828a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1055, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:05\", \"token_count\": 453, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-21\\n\\n# Slack Thread: AES-256 Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:20] Bob**: Moving forward with the AES-256 pipeline now that the crypto eval settled on it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:28] Bob**: Merged it — every temp file in the processing queue is now encrypted with a per-session key.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:37] Diana**: Running a stress test. What happens if the system loses power mid-redaction? Does the encrypted temp file persist?\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:38] Bob**: Yes, but it's useless without the session key, which only lives in volatile memory. On reboot, the cleanup hook wipes it anyway.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:39] Diana**: Makes sense.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:23] Diana**: Crypto sign-off done. Verified the `/tmp/cipherdoc` data is unreadable without the session key.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:41] Diana**: This also builds on the fail-closed work — the pipeline integrates with that deletion behavior cleanly.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:43] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:44] Alice**: Nice. :white_check_mark:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 21 slack thread ae 256 encrypt pipelin channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 05 last activ 2026 08 07 2026 08 05 09 20 bob move forward with the ae 256 pipelin now that the crypto eval settl on it 2026 08 05 09 28 bob merg it everi temp file in the process queue is now encrypt with a per session key 2026 08 05 09 37 diana run a stress test what happen if the system lose power mid redact doe the encrypt temp file persist 2026 08 05 09 38 bob yes but it s useless without the session key which onli life in volatil memori on reboot the cleanup hook wipe it anyway 2026 08 05 09 39 diana make sens 2026 08 07 13 23 diana crypto sign off done verifi the tmp cipherdoc data is unread without the session key 2026 08 07 13 41 diana this also build on the fail close work the pipelin integr with that delet behavior clean 2026 08 07 13 43 bob call this done 2026 08 07 13 44 alic nice white _ check _ mark\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8df32f68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-05-aes256-pipeline.md\", \"id\": \"02d97ea3a8ab863b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.248830354102291, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05737705014613004, \"vector_similarity\": 0.69555473, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-05-aes256-pipeline.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8df32f68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-05-aes256-pipeline.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-05-aes256-pipeline.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1112, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:37\", \"token_count\": 352, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## Sign-off Basis\\n\\nSecurity sign-off on the AES-256 at-rest pipeline was withheld until the fail-closed deletion behavior for interrupted redaction runs (T015) was confirmed Completed — an unencrypted partial output left on disk after a crash would have undermined the encryption guarantee entirely. With that dependency cleared, the sign-off proceeded against the pipeline as implemented.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## What Was Reviewed\\n\\n- AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption applied to every redacted output file before it is written to its final location.\\n\\n- Key handling confined to process memory; no plaintext key material written to disk or logs.\\n\\n- Confirmed the pipeline degrades safely (refuses to write plaintext) if key material is unavailable, consistent with the fail-closed contract from T015.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## Follow-up Noted at Sign-off\\n\\nOn machines without a hardware TPM, the volume key is still derived from a user passphrase via PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 at 100k iterations. This is not a blocker for the AES-256 pipeline sign-off itself, but Diana flagged it as a hardening follow-up: moving to Argon2id would meaningfully raise the cost of offline brute-force against weak passphrases on non-TPM hardware.\\n\\n*Status*: AES-256 at-rest pipeline signed off as Completed. Passphrase-derived key hardening (Argon2id) tracked separately as a pre-v1.0 hardening item, not a sign-off condition.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 sign off basi secur sign off on the ae 256 at rest pipelin wa withheld until the fail close delet behavior for interrupt redact run t015 wa confirm complet an unencrypt partial output left on disk after a crash would have undermin the encrypt guarante entir with that depend clear the sign off proceed against the pipelin a implement sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 what wa review ae 256 gcm authent encrypt appli to everi redact output file befor it is written to it final locat key handl confin to process memori no plaintext key materi written to disk or log confirm the pipelin degrad safe refus to write plaintext if key materi is unavail consist with the fail close contract from t015 sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 follow up note at sign off on machin without a hardwar tpm the volum key is still deriv from a user passphras via pbkdf2 hmac sha256 at 100k iter this is not a blocker for the ae 256 pipelin sign off itself but diana flag it a a harden follow up move to argon2id would meaning rais the cost of offlin brute forc against weak passphras on non tpm hardwar status ae 256 at rest pipelin sign off a complet passphras deriv key harden argon2id track separ a a pre v1 0 harden item not a sign off condit\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e99eb05e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"id\": \"3d30fbd4bb571642\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.244818127102291, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05737705014613004, \"vector_similarity\": 0.68218064, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e99eb05e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1518, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:57\", \"token_count\": 466, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-37\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-37\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-37\\n\\n**Title**: Validate batch runs under a network-denied harness\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nBuild a reproducible offline test harness that denies network access, then execute a full batch run under it to validate the strict air-gapped claim, depending on the completed AES-256 encryption pipeline. The offline batch run completed and was signed off, with a noted 45-second remote licence-check hang recorded; this sign-off is preliminary only and is not a compliance certification.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-37\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-37\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-37\\n\\n**Title**: Validate batch runs under a network-denied harness\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Offline test 